# wasm: Plan 9's C for p9web (WebAssembly, wasm32), by clang, as 8c is the 386's. The headers
# are named from the tree's root, =/ (clang's --sysroot): / on p9web, the plan9 tree on a host
# (mk/defs reads CFLAGS and LDFLAGS from here, and adds --sysroot). A program is linked against
# its libraries' archives and libc's, with procfork, rfork's RFPROC (libc/wasm/sys.c), then made
# able to fork by asyncify, at the imports a process's stack unwinds through (p9web.fork; a
# threaded program's fiber imports too).
CC=clang
LD=clang
O=w
AS=
CFLAGS=--target=wasm32 -msimd128 -nostdinc -nostdlib -isystem =/wasm/include -isystem =/sys/include -O2 -mno-extended-const -fno-builtin -fms-extensions -Xclang -fwchar-type=int -Xclang -fno-signed-wchar -fwrapv -mllvm -wasm-enable-sjlj -mllvm -wasm-use-legacy-eh=true -Wno-everything -Werror=implicit-function-declaration
LDFLAGS=--target=wasm32 -nostdlib -Wl,--allow-multiple-definition -Wl,--export-memory -Wl,--export=__stack_pointer -Wl,--export=__heap_base -Wl,-z,stack-size=1048576 -Wl,--undefined=procfork
ASYNCIFY=wasm-opt -O2 --asyncify
